Title: Loopback
Credit: A show in nine cues

INT. THE HUB - NIGHT

Each cue's family block names the members it asks something of. The hub hands each its part: pushed to a member at its own address, read by a page that follows the hub, or handed by a call to a member the hub hosts.

The house opens. A clock waits at zero.

PERFORMER
Count me in.

The metronome has no device yet, and says so. The cue goes on without it.

The band plays the second tune.

The rack, of another family, is offered to the hub and refused.

A stagehand plugs in the metronome's device.

PERFORMER
Here comes the solo.

carlos falls over.

carlos is back, and is someone new.

The stagehand holds every part to the contract.

The curtain falls.
